CORE
JmlThisField
--function JmlThisField.bump --jml-source src/main/java/JmlThisField.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for `this.field` JML access.

JML expressions of the form `this.counter` parse to a
`jml_field_access` exprt with a `this` symbol receiver. The
resolver in jml_lowering.cpp:
  1. Recognises bare `this` as the method's instance-method
     `this` parameter (`<method_id>::this`).
  2. Resolves `jml_field_access(this, counter)` to a
     `member_exprt(deref(this), counter, fieldType)` by
     looking up the field on the class's struct components
     (walking up the inheritance chain via the synthetic
     `@<Parent>` super-class component).
  3. Propagates the resolved field's type back to wrapper
     expressions (\old, +, etc.) whose default type was nil.
